<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    SLIME_GENE_ARCHIVE_BUILD_1 — the campaign gene archive.

    This is the swap the universal mod's own header describes
    (src/RimMandrake/GelatinousSlime/Defs/GeneArchiveDefs/DefaultArchive.xml):
    "the RUT layer swaps the campaign's frozen SW gene lists in by shipping
    its own GeneArchiveDef with a HIGHER priority; Dialog_GeneArchive reads
    whichever archive wins." Verified against the actual mechanism before
    authoring this (GeneArchiveDef.Active in
    src/RimMandrake/GelatinousSlime/Source/GeneArchive.cs): it iterates
    every loaded GeneArchiveDef with a non-empty targetGenes and keeps
    whichever has the highest `priority` — this def's priority of 100
    against the default's 0 is a clean, unambiguous win, gated only by the
    "prefer higher-priority archive" mod setting (on by default) added to
    SlimeMod alongside this build.

    Source is design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_slime_gene_lists.md,
    FROZEN 2026-09-07, owner-ACCEPTED 2026-09-06. 33 targets (A1-A22,
    A24-A34; A23 battle premonition is STRUCK, owner ruling, and is
    genuinely absent below — not an oversight) and all 25 riders (B1-B25,
    including the owner-commissioned B25 "The Reek"). Every GeneDef named
    below (bar A34) is authored in
    src/RimMandrake/GelatinousSlime/Defs/GeneDefs/SlimeGenes_AList.xml and
    SlimeGenes_BList.xml — read those files' headers for how each gift/cost
    is priced and where a sheet entry was narrowed to the nearest real
    field. A34 reuses the mod's own pre-existing RM_Gene_SlimeResistance
    (SlimeGenes.xml) rather than a duplicate, per the sheet's own framing
    of it as "the ironic entry".

    ⛔ Never edit DefaultArchive.xml to make this visible sooner or to
    "clean it up" — it is the universal-mod fallback for every OTHER
    campaign and mod that loads GelatinousSlime, and it is meant to lose
    here on priority, not be removed.
  -->

  <RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.GeneArchiveDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.gelatinousslime,Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">
    <defName>RUT_SlimeGeneArchive</defName>
    <label>the Ash'karr archive</label>
    <description>Everything that has ever touched the body on this world — every visitor the currents carried in, every local thing that grew to answer it. Still in circulation.</description>
    <priority>100</priority>

    <!-- A1-A22: from the visitors. A23 (battle premonition) STRUCK. -->
